{
  "inShort": "The checkpoint is at risk: neither the playable slice nor five-player testing is evidenced. It is unknown what got done in the game, because no playable build or game footage was shown. This evidence gap is common and can be fixed within this checkpoint.",
  "discussed": [
    {
      "itemId": "cmvuoyivb01awtvz8v6fyg2xh",
      "text": "The public Godot demo repository matches the task. It supplies source examples, not evidence that this game's tide or co-op sailing works."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvuoyj2j01axtvz8lc3mdzjj",
      "text": "The animated reference video remains done. Its title and thumbnail identify Big Buck Bunny. The video was not watched, so its suitability as an animated style reference remains unverified."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvuoyj5x01aytvz8lsr5pz2m",
      "text": "The Wikipedia playtesting article matches the promised reference. It explains testing methods but does not show that five players tested the game."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvuoyj7c01aztvz8t0jcex56",
      "text": "The private design board remains done. Its contents were not inspected, so it cannot establish a chosen style here."
    }
  ],
  "notDiscussed": [
    "cmvuoyj7w01b0tvz86u0a9ezv"
  ],
  "outsidePlan": [
    "The devlog reports a second island and reef damage. Those could advance the slice and sailing, but neither was demonstrated. The image shows a mountain landscape, not a tide loop. The linked video's title and thumbnail identify Big Buck Bunny, not gameplay; the video was not watched."
  ],
  "questions": [
    "Can the two-island slice and five-player test fit the remaining time at the confirmed hours?",
    "What playable evidence supports the reported second island and reef damage?",
    "Does the art reference represent a chosen style, or only one candidate?"
  ],
  "lenses": {
    "marketing": "Devlog #2 announced the second island and reef damage, with 0 applause and 0 views; the project lists no store page or game link.",
    "team": "Only Alex's 10–15 weekly hours are quantified, giving 40–60 hours across the checkpoint. Mia confirmed week one but not week two, leaving programming capacity for tide and co-op sailing uncertain.",
    "management": "The published prototype devlog meets the stage's sole exit requirement, but the four closed preparation tasks prove neither core play nor a chosen style. Publish an openable two-island build showing the tide loop and co-op sailing for five-player testing."
  }
}

